<!-- Cover Section -->
<div class="document-title">Brand Book & Philosophy</div>
<div class="accent-bar"></div>
<p style="color: #666666; font-size: 14px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;">Version 2.0 - Typography Update</p>

<!-- Content -->
<h2>1. The Vision & Purpose</h2>
<h3>Why We Exist</h3>
<p>Ideomint is not a traditional marketing agency. We are a <strong>Creative Experience Company</strong>. The ambition is to build a culturally relevant institution that sits at the intersection of brand strategy, live experiences, original media, and community building. We exist to give creativity a purpose.</p>

<h2>2. The Naming Story</h2>
<p>The name <strong>Ideomint</strong> was engineered to instantly provoke curiosity while revealing a deeply intelligent story.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>IDEO (The Raw Material):</strong> Represents the initial thought, the imagination, and the visionary spark.</li>
  <li><strong>MINT (The Execution):</strong> Represents the rigorous process of forging something of immense, tangible value (like minting a coin). It signifies flawless execution.</li>
</ul>
<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>The Official Tagline:</strong><br>
  Exceptional Ideas. Flawlessly Minted.
</div>

<h2>3. Typography & Voice (New)</h2>
<p>Our typographic personality is rooted in modern editorial design—bold, highly legible, and unpretentious. A brand is recognized not just by its logo, but by the exact shape of the letters it uses across all mediums.</p>

<h3>Master Brand Fonts</h3>
<table class="content-table">
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Font Family</th>
    <th style="width: 20%;">Primary Use Case</th>
    <th style="width: 55%;">Psychology & Rules</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Satoshi</strong><br>(Geometric Sans-Serif)</td>
    <td>Headlines & Display Titles</td>
    <td>Satoshi is our "shouting" font. It is bold, structured, and modern. We use it strictly for massive headlines and the Ideomint wordmark. It must always be used in heavily weighted forms (Bold 700 or Black 900) to convey authority.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Manrope</strong><br>(Clean Sans-Serif)</td>
    <td>Body Text & UI Labels</td>
    <td>Manrope is our "conversational" font. It is highly legible. We use it for paragraphs, letters, legal documents, and digital interface labels. It strips away arrogance and makes us feel approachable and human.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>Typographic Color Rules</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>When writing on White/Canvas backgrounds:</strong> All headings must be Midnight Ink (<span class="hex">#05070D</span>). We do not use pure black.</li>
  <li><strong>When writing on Dark backgrounds:</strong> All headings must be Pure White (<span class="hex">#FFFFFF</span>).</li>
  <li><strong>The "Spark" Accent:</strong> We only use Creative Flame (<span class="hex">#FF5A3C</span>) to highlight <strong>one single, powerful word</strong> inside a headline. We never make an entire sentence orange. This creates dramatic tension and draws the eye instantly.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. The Color Architecture</h2>
<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>Usage Ratio:</strong><br>
  The brand must always maintain a premium, dark, editorial feel across digital spaces. The ideal color distribution is <strong>70% Foundation</strong> (Midnight Ink), <strong>20% Typography/Space</strong> (Human Canvas), and exactly <strong>10% Accent</strong> (Creative Flame).
</div>

<h3>The Foundation Colors</h3>
<table class="content-table">
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Color Name</th>
    <th style="width: 15%;">HEX Code</th>
    <th style="width: 60%;">Psychology & Usage</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Midnight Ink</strong></td>
    <td><span class="hex">#05070D</span></td>
    <td><strong>Authority & Premium Depth.</strong> Primary background color.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Human Canvas</strong></td>
    <td><span class="hex">#F6F1E8</span></td>
    <td><strong>Warmth & Accessibility.</strong> Secondary background and typography.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>The Division Accents</h3>
<table class="content-table">
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Division</th>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Accent Color</th>
    <th style="width: 15%;">HEX Code</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Psychology & Usage</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Ideomint Studio</strong></td>
    <td>Creative Flame</td>
    <td><span class="hex">#FF5A3C</span></td>
    <td><strong>Energy & Action.</strong> The master brand accent.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Ideomint Live</strong></td>
    <td>Signal Lime</td>
    <td><span class="hex">#C7F36B</span></td>
    <td><strong>Youth & Nightlife.</strong> High energy cultural relevance.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Ideomint Raw</strong></td>
    <td>Digital Pulse</td>
    <td><span class="hex">#5B5AF7</span></td>
    <td><strong>Transparency.</strong> Electric blue for building in public.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

